    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing high-ceiling speed and favorable matchups against vulnerable arms. **Corbin Carroll** leads the pack with an elite score of 83.53, benefiting from a prime #2 hole placement and a favorable encounter with Holmes. While the Elite Hold SP factor provides a marginal 4% drag on his stolen base potential, his raw projection remains unmatched. Supporting him, **Josh Naylor** (73.37) and **Mickey Moniak** (68.92) are our primary engines against the soft rotations of Wesneski and Webb, respectively. **Moniak** in particular is a standout play, as his high score is bolstered by a +5% wind-out advantage and an ideal platoon alignment that maximizes his current power-speed profile.\n\nThe bench remains constrained by a heavy injury toll, notably the absence of **James Wood** and **Vinnie Pasquantino**. Among the healthy assets, **Jose Caballero** was the most difficult exclusion; despite a solid base projection that would typically command a start, his current bench status and a -13% platoon disadvantage against the right-handed Fisher pushed his score below the floor threshold. Elsewhere, we are leaning into favorable park environments for **Henry Bolte** and **Max Muncy** against Gore; both receive a +10% park boost that helps mitigate the risks associated with the lower end of the batting order. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Travis Bazzana** (42.21), whose marginal score is suppressed by a negative platoon split against the left-handed Peralta, leaving him on the absolute edge of our active rotation.",
